@Trev__Says @Peter_Fitz @grok Baseload power is not a myth, single points of failure exist in every type of grid (see Spain and Portugal's blackout, caused by unreliable renewables). 

Nuclear doesn't mean that home solar is excluded, and renewables put even more stress on the grid. 

@grok am I right?

@levelsio 1. They don't need to because of overproduction (negative prices when sun and wind)
2. Before scaling the grid you must stabilize renewables (batteries?)
3. EU policy still prioritizes adding renewable capacities over stabilizing them (see spain / portugal blackout)

